es ran and passed.\n\nChanges:\n- **`src/click/termui.py`**: added `import os`. Updated the `filename` annotation in the third overload and the implementation. The body now wraps the value in a tuple when it is a `str` or `os.PathLike`. The docstring has the new sentence and a `versionchanged:: 8.5.0` entry.\n- **`src/click/_termui_impl.py`**: `Editor.edit_files` takes `Iterable[str | os.PathLike[str]]`. I left the body alone, since `Popen` already handles path objects and the tests confirm it.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: added the entry at the end of the Unreleased list, with `{issue}2869` and `{pr}3781`.\n\nTwo checks didn't run. The typing test `tests/typing/typing_edit.py` is not part of the spec's command list, and mypy, pyright and ruff are not installed in `.venv`, so I didn't run it. The full pytest suite passes (1991 passed, 24 skipped, 1 xfailed), though 31000 tests were deselected by the project's pytest config. I did not commit.", "ttft_ms": 1397, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 27400, "uuid": "a35587de-99b8-4b83-bc2a-e4e6901b6eaa", "ttft_stream_ms": 1170, "time_to_request_ms": 233, "first_content_frame_ms": 1170, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
